        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Lake Trasimene</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">21 June 217 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The north shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-trasimeno">Lake Trasimene</a>, south of Cortona, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruria">Etruria</a> (modern Tuscany, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>); the shoreline has changed since</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and its allies under the consul Gaius Flaminius, about 25,000 men in four legions, two Roman and two allied; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and its Gallic, Iberian and African troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>, usually assumed to number more than 50,000</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Roman army was ambushed and nearly all of it was killed or captured; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a> and Fabius Pictor give 15,000 killed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-fabius-maximus">Quintus Fabius Maximus</a> dictator.</span></div>
        </div>
